  "body_html": "<h1>Single Positive Depth Theta Lift of Data</h1>\n<p>Let \\(\\Sigma=(x,\\Gamma,\\phi,\\rho)\\) be a single positive-depth block of depth \\(r=2s\\) for \\(G=U(V)\\). The target hermitian space is the isometry class of \\(V_\\Gamma\\). Choose \\(w\\in V\\otimes_D V_\\Gamma\\) such that\n\\[\nM(w)=\\Gamma.\n\\]\nDefine the target lattice function by\n\\[\nL'_t=wL_{t+s},\n\\]\nand let \\(x'\\) be the corresponding building point. Set\n\\[\n\\Gamma'=M'(w).\n\\]\nConjugation by \\(w\\) gives an isomorphism between the relevant centralizers, and the target character and cuspidal finite quotient representation are the transported contragredients:\n\\[\n\\phi'=\\phi^\\ast ∘ \\alpha^{-1},\\qquad\n\\rho'=\\rho^\\ast ∘ \\alpha^{-1}.\n\\]\nThe resulting datum\n\\[\n\\Sigma'=(x',\\Gamma',\\phi',\\rho')\n\\]\nis well-defined up to equivalence, independent of the representative of \\([\\Sigma]\\) and of the choice of \\(w\\). Its equivalence class is denoted \\(\\#^+([\\Sigma])\\).</p>",
  "proof_html": null,
